  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full two-hour set at the Teragram Ballroom in Los Angeles on December 14, 2025, captured in a matrix recording that blends soundboard audio with audience microphones [1]. This is the 451st archived show for the band, following a previous performance at the same venue the day before [2]. The setlist features several rare tracks, including “Armies of the Lord” and “Cold at Night,” which have limited archives [1]. Notable bustouts include “Rotten Stinking Mouthpiece” and “Song for Black Sabbath's Second North American Tour,” both of which had not been played in over four years [1]. The band also performed “For the Krishnacore Bands,” a song absent from the archive for roughly two years [1]. Nicole Lawrence joined the stage for pedal steel and guitar during the first half of the show [1]. The encore included “Let Me Bathe in Demonic Light,” “No Children,” “International Small Arms Traffic Blues,” and the mythically rare “Sweet Jane” [1]. The uploader noted that the venue charged a steep recording fee, which was covered by fan contributions to ensure these shows were preserved [1]. The recording was taped by Kyle Kennelly and Emerald Green, with the transfer handled by Kennelly [1].",
